# A column whose types do not widen is DS2003; the column gets the error type, so nothing else is reported.
mode: check
show: schema
schema: 'a.csv'(x: long, y: string); 'b.csv'(x: string)
---- query
from 'a.csv' | union 'b.csv' | where x > 1
---- expected
error[DS2003]: `union` cannot combine column `x` of types `long` and `string`
  --> query:1:22
  |
1 | from 'a.csv' | union 'b.csv' | where x > 1
  |                      ^^^^^^^ here `x` is `string`
  |
  = help: convert it to one type before the `union`: `union (from 'b.csv' | extend x = tolong(x))`
  = note: before this table, `x` is `long` (read from a.csv)

query 1 columns:
  x: (error)
  y: string
